    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Deﬁnition 4. For each j ∈ J , we deﬁne Ij = i∈I Iij. Also, let Sij′ = Sij ∩ Ij, ∀i ∈ I and ∀j ∈ J . Corollary 4. Let i ∈ I and j ∈ J . If Sij′ = ∅, then Sij′ is as one of the forms of Sij′ = {Lj}, Sij′ = {Uj}, Sij′ = {Lj,Uj} or Sij′ = [Lj,Uj], where Lj and Uj are the lower and upper bound of Ij = [Lj,Uj], respectively. Proof. From Deﬁnition 4 and Remark 3, we have"
