    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Hence, for each i ∈ I , if Lij ∈ Ij (Uij ∈ Ij), then we must have Lij = Lj (Uij = Uj). On the other hand, from Remark 3, a non-empty Sij is as one of the forms of Sij = {Lij}, Sij = {Uij}, Sij = {Lij,Uij} or Sij = [Lij,Uij]. So, if Sij = {Lij} and Sij′ = Sij ∩ Ij = ∅, then Lij ∈ Ij; that is, Lij = Lj and therefore Sij′ = Sij ∩ Ij = {Lj}. For the other cases, the results are attained by the similar argument."
